From c42877005d0b4f0a44116fda2e0263b8655a5e6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim 'mithro' Ansell <me@mith.ro>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 22:38:22 +0930
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GENET TX: wrap the 16-bit consumer index

bcm2838_genet_tx() walks TX descriptors while cons_index_fld !=
prod_index_fld. Both start as the 16-bit INDEX fields of the
PROD_INDEX/CONS_INDEX registers, but cons_index_fld was incremented as
a plain uint32_t. When the guest's producer index wraps from 0xffff to
0 while the consumer is still at 0xfffe/0xffff, cons_index_fld counts
on to 0x10000, 0x10001, ... and never equals the small producer value
again until it wraps at 2^32: the loop keeps reading descriptors while
holding the BQL, so the main loop (serial, monitor, net backends) and
the other vCPUs block behind it and the whole guest freezes.

Seen in fpgas.online-infra's VM CI: every run froze the virtual Pi
after its 65536th TX descriptor on a ring (~30 verify-pi tasks, ~5 min
of SSH traffic), reported as "No route to host". gdb on the frozen
process: CPU 2/TCG in bcm2838_genet_tx(ring_index=4, cons_index=65534)
across samples, every other thread in qemu_mutex_lock(&bql).

Wrap the consumer index with the same FIELD_EX32 used to extract it.
---
 hw/net/bcm2838_genet.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/net/bcm2838_genet.c b/hw/net/bcm2838_genet.c
index 476f692..b3fecad 100644
--- a/hw/net/bcm2838_genet.c
+++ b/hw/net/bcm2838_genet.c
@@ -493,7 +493,15 @@ static uint64_t bcm2838_genet_tx(BCM2838GenetState *s, unsigned int ring_index,
         }
 
         num_descs++;
-        cons_index_fld++;
+        /*
+         * PROD_INDEX/CONS_INDEX are 16-bit counters: wrap like the hardware.
+         * Left to count past 0xffff in 32 bits, cons_index_fld never equals
+         * a prod_index_fld that has just wrapped to a small value, and this
+         * loop spins (holding the BQL) for ~2^32 descriptors -- the whole VM
+         * froze after the guest's 65536th TX descriptor on a ring.
+         */
+        cons_index_fld = FIELD_EX32(cons_index_fld + 1,
+                                    GENET_DMA_CONS_INDEX, INDEX);
         s->regs.tdma.descs[desc_index].length_status =
             FIELD_DP32(s->regs.tdma.descs[desc_index].length_status,
                        GENET_RDMA_LENGTH_STATUS, OWN, 1);
